From 3884682508e86a937e8aed914c29a26907fec5f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:46:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/91] fix: harden beacon listener rate limiting and thread
 start; tighten tests

- Check the per-source bucket before spending a global token, so one noisy
  unpinned host cannot empty the budget that admits new peers.
- For pinned sources, spend the per-source token only on structurally valid
  beacons; junk forged with a known peer's IP is charged to the global bucket
  and can no longer expire that peer.
- Create the worker thread before marking the listener running; a thread
  creation failure is reported in /health instead of escaping Server::run().
- server_endpoints: inject via the interface's directed broadcast, gate socket
  assertions to Linux, assert the self filter on port+source and make the port
  release check able to fail.
- server_cli2: scan still receives the loopback beacon with beacon_listen on.
- Document that the listener is not interface-scoped (WAN on double NAT).

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5.5
